@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam backgroundcolor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor white
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor white

title UML Activity Diagram (v2) – Blockchain-Enabled IoT System for Produce Traceability and Cold Chain Monitoring\n(Resolves DR-01, DR-02, DR-03, DR-04, DR-06)

|Supply Chain Operator|
start
:Register produce batch\n(type, quantity, origin, destination, harvest date);

|System|
:Validate input;
:Generate opaque Batch ID\nand QR identifier;
:Store batch and traceability record;
:Submit BATCH_REGISTERED hash\nfor anchoring (see anchoring sub-flow);
:Display QR code;

|Supply Chain Operator|
:Attach IoT device to batch;

|System|
:Verify device is ACTIVE\nand has no active assignment;
:Create DEVICE_ASSIGNMENT;

repeat
  |IoT Device (ESP32 + DHT22)|
  :Read temperature and humidity;
  if (Sensor values valid?) then (yes)
    :Package reading with\ntimestamp and Device ID;
    :Send reading with device API key;
    |System|
    :Authenticate device and validate payload;
    :Resolve batch from active DEVICE_ASSIGNMENT;
    :Store reading in off-chain database;
    :Evaluate thresholds for the batch's\nproduce type (breach / recovery counters);
    if (Excursion opened or closed?) then (yes)
      :Create or close ALERT\nand COLD_CHAIN_EVENT;
      :Send alert to operator dashboard;
      :Build canonical payload hash\nand create BLOCKCHAIN_RECORD (PENDING);
      |Blockchain Network|
      :Receive anchoring transaction;
      if (Transaction confirmed?) then (yes)
        |System|
        :Store transaction hash,\nset status CONFIRMED;
      else (no)
        |System|
        :Set status FAILED, log error,\nschedule retry;
      endif
    else (no)
      :Continue monitoring\n(readings are NOT anchored);
    endif
  else (no)
    :Discard reading and log sensor error;
  endif
  |IoT Device (ESP32 + DHT22)|
  :Wait for next sampling interval;
repeat while (Batch active and device assigned?) is (yes) not (no)

|Supply Chain Operator|
:Close batch on delivery;

|System|
:Unassign device;
:(Optional) Anchor BATCH_CLOSED with\nMerkle root of batch readings;
stop

note right
  Anchoring sub-flow (above) is reused by:
  - BATCH_REGISTERED
  - MOVEMENT
  - COLD_CHAIN_EVENT
  - EXCURSION_OPENED / EXCURSION_CLOSED
  - BATCH_CLOSED
  Raw readings are never written on-chain (DR-02).
  Network: public testnet (Polygon Amoy) (DR-04).
end note

caption Figure 5 (v2): UML Activity Diagram
@enduml
